# Non-circular gear pair, driven through the packaged FreeCAD 1.1.3.
#
#   reprocad record ~/dev/freecad.noncirculargears/tests/noncircular-gears.steps \
#       --binary /usr/bin/freecad --profile noncircular
#
# The profile is a saved home whose Mod directory links to this workbench, so
# the run loads it the way an installed addon is loaded.
#
# Two things are on screen rather than asserted: the pair appears meshed at one
# click, and editing f(x) in the property editor rebuilds both gears - the
# second gear is derived from the first, so it has to follow.
#
# Axonometric is a submenu, not a view: stopping on it leaves the whole View
# menu open over the tree, and every step after it aims at a covered screen.

note step 1 - a new document
menu File > New Document for:40
sleep 6

note step 2 - switch to the Non-Circular Gear workbench
menu View > Workbench > Non-Circular Gear for:40
sleep 8

note step 3 - one command builds both gears
menu Non-Circular Gear > Gear Pair for:40
sleep 10
menu View > Standard views > Axonometric > Isometric for:40
sleep 3
menu View > Standard views > Fit all for:40
sleep 5

note step 4 - select the driving gear; the second one is derived from it
clickon NonCircularGear in:0,150,420,90 for:40
sleep 5

note step 5 - what the pair came out at: the ratio really does vary over the turn
scroll 200 800 -8
sleep 2
waittext max ratio in:0,520,420,420 for:40
sleep 8

note step 6 - a different f(x): three lobes instead of one
scroll 200 800 8
sleep 2
field function in:0,520,420,420 for:40
sleep 2
key ctrl+a
type 1 + 0.5 * cos(3 * x)
key Return
sleep 12
menu View > Standard views > Fit all for:40
sleep 8

note step 7 - from above, both gears rebuilt and still meshed
menu View > Standard views > Top for:40
sleep 4
move 700 900
sleep 8
